WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.621
From an engine to a learner.

2
00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:07.320
Last lesson you built the engine: a Value that records operations and backpropagates.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.144
This lesson, covering the second half of the lecture, turns it into something that learns.

4
00:00:12.424 --> 00:00:13.597
The steps are few.

5
00:00:13.877 --> 00:00:18.037
A neuron is a weighted sum plus a bias, passed through a nonlinearity.

6
00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:23.736
A layer is a list of neurons; a multilayer perceptron (MLP) is a list of layers.

7
00:00:24.016 --> 00:00:28.389
A loss function measures how wrong the network’s predictions are, as one number.

8
00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:33.256
Backpropagation gives the gradient of that number with respect to every weight.

9
00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:37.312
Gradient descent nudges every weight a little against its gradient.

10
00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:38.403
Repeat.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:41.029
Nothing in that list needs new calculus.

12
00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:48.925
A neural network, for this lecture’s purposes, is just a big expression, and you already know how to differentiate big expressions.

13
00:00:49.205 --> 00:00:54.987
The new ideas are about what you differentiate (the loss), and what you do with the gradient (the update).
